our flight getting canceled,

00:48:30.850 --> 00:48:33.160
because every day there's
more flights getting canceled

00:48:33.160 --> 00:48:34.960
as we get closer and closer to this time.

00:48:34.960 --> 00:48:37.390
Also, I'm worried about
getting stuck in Mexico,

00:48:37.390 --> 00:48:38.770
and thinking about what am I gonna do

00:48:38.770 --> 00:48:40.380
if we have to stay extra time in Mexico.

00:48:40.380 --> 00:48:42.080
Am I gonna have to stay an extra week?

00:48:42.080 --> 00:48:44.200
I'm not gonna like, what
if it's one of our kids?

00:48:44.200 --> 00:48:45.487
I'm not gonna be like,

00:48:45.487 --> 00:48:46.720
"We asked to stay here because one

00:48:46.720 --> 00:48:48.519
of my kids has tested positive."

00:48:48.519 --> 00:48:50.760
Again, it wasn't the fear of the illness,

00:48:50.760 --> 00:48:53.271
it was the fear of the logical

00:48:53.271 --> 00:48:56.670
or the logistical implications
of somebody getting it.

00:48:56.670 --> 00:48:57.630
Yeah.

00:48:57.630 --> 00:48:58.960
And Jessie was saying the whole time,

00:48:58.960 --> 00:49:00.770
she was like, "I think we
should cancel the trip,

00:49:00.770 --> 00:49:02.560
because you're gonna be too anxious,

00:49:02.560 --> 00:49:03.859
and you're not gonna be
able to enjoy yourself,

00:49:03.859 --> 00:49:04.692
because you're gonna be worried
about us getting stuck."

00:49:04.692 --> 00:49:07.290
It's just the logistical
stuff is the kind of thing

00:49:07.290 --> 00:49:09.166
that I get anxiety about.

00:49:09.166 --> 00:49:11.090
And so I was like,
"Well, you're not wrong,

00:49:11.090 --> 00:49:12.810
but let's do it, we're doing this."

00:49:12.810 --> 00:49:14.690
You know, it's not really any less safe

00:49:14.690 --> 00:49:16.170
there than it is here, and like,

00:49:16.170 --> 00:49:18.070
let's just stay committed to the plan.

00:49:19.220 --> 00:49:22.590
And then my brother
tests positive for COVID,

00:49:22.590 --> 00:49:24.490
which was happening, so many,

00:49:24.490 --> 00:49:26.410
if you don't know somebody
who tested positive for COVID

00:49:26.410 --> 00:49:27.375
in the past couple of weeks,

00:49:27.375 --> 00:49:29.630
then I don't know who you
are and where you live,

00:49:29.630 --> 00:49:32.750
but like it's happening everywhere.

00:49:32.750 --> 00:49:34.163
And of course I had spent,

00:49:35.010 --> 00:49:36.900
I had been with my brother at dinner,

00:49:36.900 --> 00:49:39.220
went to his house, sat
on the couch next to him.

00:49:39.220 --> 00:49:41.560
Like, I just basically just been breathing

00:49:41.560 --> 00:49:45.630
the same air with him just
multiple days in a row.

00:49:45.630 --> 00:49:47.507
You were doing that thing to
each other where it's like,

00:49:47.507 --> 00:49:48.733
"Does my breath stink?"

00:49:49.997 --> 00:49:51.588
And then he was like, "Well,
does my breath stink?"

00:49:51.588 --> 00:49:54.700
And then you're like, "Yes,
but does mine stink more?"

00:49:54.700 --> 00:49:55.550
Yeah, exactly,

00:49:55.550 --> 00:49:56.410
breathing each other's air.

00:49:56.410 --> 00:49:58.720
And then an hour later,
you do it all again.

00:49:58.720 --> 00:49:59.553
Right.

00:49:59.553 --> 00:50:00.470
What about now, "Does my breath stink?"

00:50:00.470 --> 00:50:02.327
And it was happening
with every family member.

00:50:02.327 --> 00:50:04.287
"Does your breath stink?"

00:50:04.287 --> 00:50:05.120
And so, okay.

00:50:05.120 --> 00:50:06.192
Listen, I don't know.

00:50:06.192 --> 00:50:10.992
I ended up getting all
five symptoms of Omicron,

00:50:10.992 --> 00:50:12.800
like the ones that were listed

00:50:12.800 --> 00:50:14.120
as the five most common symptoms.

00:50:14.120 --> 00:50:16.680
I got all five symptoms, very mildly,

00:50:16.680 --> 00:50:18.400
like to the point where I
was like, is this an allergy?

00:50:18.400 --> 00:50:20.180
Is this like a cold, is this?

00:50:20.180 --> 00:50:24.330
I tested two times with
one of those rapid tests.

00:50:24.330 --> 00:50:25.733
It was both negative.

00:50:25.733 --> 00:50:27.460
Everybody kept saying-

00:50:27.460 --> 00:50:28.440
Both negative.

00:50:28.440 --> 00:50:31.270
The negative tests are much
less reliable with this,

00:50:31.270 --> 00:50:32.810
in general, and also with this strain.

00:50:32.810 --> 00:50:34.900
And then when I got
back, I got a PCR test,

00:50:34.900 --> 00:50:36.550
still negative, so.

00:50:36.550 --> 00:50:38.700
This is funny, because you're doing like,

00:50:38.700 --> 00:50:41.510
it's like, I mean, 'cause
there's still this stigma.

00:50:41.510 --> 00:50:42.343
It's like-

00:50:42.343 --> 00:50:43.670
Yeah, you leaned away from me.

00:50:43.670 --> 00:50:44.503
When people say-

00:50:44.503 --> 00:50:46.210
Trust me, you've been exposed to COVID.

00:50:46.210 --> 00:50:47.190
I'm just playing up,

00:50:47.190 --> 00:50:50.056
but when people say they've got it,

00:50:50.056 --> 00:50:54.217
there's an eroding, but
still present stigma of like,

00:50:54.217 --> 00:50:56.470
"I gotta confess, I got it.

00:50:56.470 --> 00:50:57.303
I got it."

00:50:57.303 --> 00:50:58.950
Well, but I think that's going away,

00:50:58.950 --> 00:50:59.870
but you're doing the opposite.

00:50:59.870 --> 00:51:02.930
You're like, trying to
convince me that you have it?

00:51:02.930 --> 00:51:05.090
No, well, first of all, again.

00:51:05.090 --> 00:51:06.840
I do have it, man.

00:51:06.840 --> 00:51:08.210
I'm not really thinking about

00:51:08.210 --> 00:51:09.980
the widespread implications of the things

00:51:09.980 --> 00:51:12.830
that I'm saying right now, so
please let me speak freely.

00:51:14.295 --> 00:51:16.867
But there's honestly, there
was a part of me that was like,

00:51:16.867 --> 00:51:19.120
"I want to get this to
get it over with it,

00:51:19.120 --> 00:51:20.820
'cause I'm so tired of worrying about it."

00:51:20.820 --> 00:51:22.690
And everybody that I know
that is double vaxxed

00:51:22.690 --> 00:51:24.900
that's getting it is
having such mild symptoms,

00:51:24.900 --> 00:51:27.320
and I'm like, "Just give me the damn virus

00:51:27.320 --> 00:51:28.550
so I can get through this,

00:51:28.550 --> 00:51:30.350
and not have to think about it anymore."

00:51:30.350 --> 00:51:31.390
So you do feel-

00:51:31.390 --> 00:51:33.300
Right or wrong, that's what I was feeling.

00:51:33.300 --> 00:51:36.325
And so you're airing,

00:51:36.325 --> 00:51:38.920
you're leaning towards concluding

00:51:38.920 --> 00:51:39.923
that you had it.
My brother.

00:51:41.098 --> 00:51:43.710
But you're leaning towards
concluding that you had it,

00:51:43.710 --> 00:51:45.260
because that gives you peace of mind.

00:51:45.260 --> 00:51:46.610
No, I...

00:51:46.610 --> 00:51:50.400
No, I'm saying that I
had all the symptoms,

00:51:50.400 --> 00:51:52.597
and all these people online are like,

00:51:52.597 --> 00:51:54.030
"These are the symptoms that I had.

00:51:54.030 --> 00:51:56.743
I'm not testing positive."

00:51:56.743 --> 00:51:58.637
And so I'm just like,

00:51:58.637 --> 00:52:00.330
"Okay, maybe I had it, maybe I didn't."

00:52:00.330 --> 00:52:02.720
I'm not behaving any
differently than I was already.

00:52:02.720 --> 00:52:03.865
I'm taking all the precautions

00:52:03.865 --> 00:52:05.011
I've been doing here at work.
But that factored into

00:52:05.011 --> 00:52:05.894
not going to Mexico.

00:52:05.894 --> 00:52:07.020
No...

00:52:07.020 --> 00:52:08.920
No, because I tested negative.

00:52:08.920 --> 00:52:10.334
And I was like, "If I test negative,

00:52:10.334 --> 00:52:12.580
and these symptoms are gone by the time

00:52:12.580 --> 00:52:13.940
we're supposed to fly, I'm going."

00:52:13.940 --> 00:52:15.510
You felt better about going?
That was the plan.

00:52:15.510 --> 00:52:16.343
Yeah.

00:52:17.250 --> 00:52:19.034
Then Shepherd,

00:52:19.034 --> 00:52:21.992
who is vaccinated, and not boosted,

00:52:21.992 --> 00:52:25.780
because he's only 13, Shepherd comes down

00:52:25.780 --> 00:52:27.950
with the exact same
symptoms as my brother,

00:52:27.950 --> 00:52:31.740
which is basically like
a pretty bad sore throat,

00:52:31.740 --> 00:52:33.090
and like some aches,

00:52:33.090 --> 00:52:35.140
and what you typically see

00:52:35.140 --> 00:52:37.120
in a vaccinated person who gets it,

00:52:37.120 --> 00:52:38.860
which is just sort of a rough cold

00:52:38.860 --> 00:52:41.133
that kind of knocks you
out for a couple of days.

00:52:42.870 --> 00:52:45.030
And so, again, we tested
him, it was negative,

00:52:45.030 --> 00:52:49.810
but at that point it
was Christmas Eve-Eve,

00:52:49.810 --> 00:52:51.307
when that happened with
Shepherd and I was like,

00:52:51.307 --> 00:52:52.810
"Okay, let's do it, let's cancel."

00:52:52.810 --> 00:52:54.310
Thankfully, we got the
money back for everything.

00:52:54.310 --> 00:52:56.480
Like, we actually didn't
have our trip insured.

00:52:56.480 --> 00:52:59.230
I thought that maybe
it was, but it wasn't,

00:52:59.230 --> 00:53:01.680
and so thank you, Jenna,

00:53:01.680 --> 00:53:04.860
for making lots of phone
calls and figuring that out,

00:53:04.860 --> 00:53:08.940
but we got our money back so
we didn't have to pay anything,

00:53:08.940 --> 00:53:12.205
and then there was sort
of a sense of relief,

00:53:12.205 --> 00:53:13.673
but then I was like, well,
what are we gonna do now?

00:53:13.673 --> 00:53:16.780
We're just gonna stay in North Carolina?

00:53:16.780 --> 00:53:18.058
Because it was,

00:53:18.058 --> 00:53:22.280
the way that COVID impacted
our family gatherings was.

00:53:22.280 --> 00:53:23.580
Okay, Shepherd's not coming over

00:53:23.580 --> 00:53:27.020
to Christmas Eve at my parents, you know?

00:53:27.020 --> 00:53:29.640
Because they're in like their mid-70's,

00:53:29.640 --> 00:53:32.420
and it's like, we're trying
to protect everybody,

00:53:32.420 --> 00:53:33.253
right?
Yeah.

00:53:33.253 --> 00:53:34.228
And so-

00:53:34.228 --> 00:53:35.061
Dejavu.

00:53:35.061 --> 00:53:35.894
And so, yeah, it was like,

00:53:35.894 --> 00:53:36.730
"Oh man, this again?

00:53:36.730 --> 00:53:37.650
We have to do this."

00:53:37.650 --> 00:53:40.830
And like Cole, my brother
couldn't come to the things.

00:53:40.830 --> 00:53:42.330
I saw him in the beginning of the trip,

00:53:42.330 --> 00:53:43.240
and I didn't see him again.

00:53:43.240 --> 00:53:44.073
That sucks.

00:53:44.073 --> 00:53:46.820
And so I was just very
frustrated by the whole thing,

00:53:46.820 --> 00:53:47.653
but I was also like.
So if you stayed.

00:53:47.653 --> 00:53:48.945
I don't want to stick around

00:53:48.945 --> 00:53:52.450
and be in this situation where, and again,

00:53:52.450 --> 00:53:54.573
we're in a place where
some people are like,

00:53:54.573 --> 00:53:56.680
think that we're crazy, right?

00:53:56.680 --> 00:54:00.150
And it's funny because
when somebody would ask us

00:54:00.150 --> 00:54:03.540
to do something through my
in-laws or through my parents,

00:54:03.540 --> 00:54:05.112
and they would be like, do
y'all want to go do this?

00:54:05.112 --> 00:54:06.600
I would literally say this.

00:54:06.600 --> 00:54:09.740
I would say, "You just tell
them that we're crazy liberals

00:54:09.740 --> 00:54:12.000
from California and were
scared of the virus.

00:54:12.000 --> 00:54:14.770
That will end the conversation,
so we don't have to,

00:54:14.770 --> 00:54:16.101
you can put it on me,

00:54:16.101 --> 00:54:17.440
'cause that's what people
think about me anyway.

00:54:17.440 --> 00:54:18.607
So just say that,

00:54:18.607 --> 00:54:20.130
and that's why we're
not going to your dinner

00:54:20.130 --> 00:54:21.250
that you've got planned or whatever.

00:54:21.250 --> 00:54:23.790
We're crazy liberals and
we're scared of the virus."

00:54:23.790 --> 00:54:25.550
And so that would just,

00:54:25.550 --> 00:54:28.570
I had to kind of deploy that
strategy a couple of times,

00:54:28.570 --> 00:54:29.780
because I didn't-
That work?

00:54:29.780 --> 00:54:31.240
Yeah, well, I just ended the conversation,

00:54:31.240 --> 00:54:32.893
'cause I don't want to get into this like,

00:54:32.893 --> 00:54:34.800
you see it this way, I see it this way,

00:54:34.800 --> 00:54:35.990
let's have an argument about it.

00:54:35.990 --> 00:54:37.700
It's like, no, you do your thing,

00:54:37.700 --> 00:54:39.150
I'll do my thing, we're good.

00:54:40.920 --> 00:54:42.010
But, I was like,

00:54:42.010 --> 00:54:45.300
I want to make something
out of this trip, right?

00:54:45.300 --> 00:54:48.630
And I don't even know
where I got the idea,

00:54:48.630 --> 00:54:49.810
but I was like-

00:54:49.810 --> 00:54:51.130
Just say I gave it to you.

00:54:51.130 --> 00:54:52.080
Well, you didn't.

00:54:54.260 --> 00:54:58.280
Cross country trip, me and Lock.

00:54:58.280 --> 00:54:59.410
Now, Lock and I have been trying

00:54:59.410 --> 00:55:01.240
to go to multiple places together

00:55:01.240 --> 00:55:02.610
over the past couple of years,

00:55:02.610 --> 00:55:04.050
